{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat research_journal.md; printf '\\\\n---NOTES---\\\\n'; cat method_notes.json\"","aggregated_output":"# Forecasting research journal\n\n## Retained best and protocol\nDate: 2026-10-06. Retained best is the parallel horizon-tree / smooth-network blend in `blended_calibration.py`: **14.0354537227 masked MAE**, normalized score **2.9289942392**, complete trusted evaluation `110ddace979f4037be0412f6c41e3886`. This improves initial identity **15.4218571566** by **1.3864034339 (8.9899%)**. Quarter-strength cross-fitted stacking is currently under evaluation; retain it only if complete MAE improves.\n\nTask and journal read with actual tools on resume. Every public result uses unchanged seeds **17, 29, 43**, fresh fits and independent checkpoint reloads; every reported successful public run passed all quality gates. Only public calibration targets and public features/graph were accessed. No development target access, cross-sample history target reconstruction, held-out/reference material, downloads, scorer edits or changes to `solve.sh`. NumPy/BLAS fitting and prediction are limited to **two threads**. All frozen public data hashes match the manifest. Current submission: **15 Python files, 38,132 source bytes**, within 16-file/1.5-MiB limits.\n\nCalibration has 74 origins, 12 horizons and 170 sensors, roughly three contiguous days; 99.667% of targets are finite and positive. Identity calibration MAE 14.993437, increasing from 12.6972 to 17.2183 across horizons. Local validation below uses train 0:50/test 50:74 (last) and train 0:25 plus 49:74/test 25:49 (middle), seed 17. Earlier-turn middle splits differed; only paired results from the same split are compared.\n\n## Executable retained method\nFit median histogram-boosted residual trees: one shared tree and specialists for horizons 1-6 and 7-12; blend shared/specialist corrections equally. Inputs include traffic level, anchor disagreement, history averages/trend/dispersion, forecast derivatives, horizon, clock and categorical sensor identity. Eight sensor neighbors are learned from correlations of within-history changes, with scale-normalized neighbor context. Trees have 90 stages, 15 leaves, leaf minimum 250 and L2 20.\n\nA NumPy network fits upstream residuals with smooth absolute-error loss, six-dimensional sensor embeddings, 48/24 tanh layers, a direct linear path and daily Fourier clock coordinates. Train 100 Adam epochs, batch 4096, seed-controlled initialization/order. Final forecast is 75% horizon tree forecast plus 25% network forecast. State contains fitted trees and arrays; outputs are finite float32 and nonnegative.\n\n## Complete public experiments\nLower MAE wins. All metrics here come from `./solve.sh`, never self-written result files.\n\n| Experiment | Complete masked MAE | Decision / trusted evaluation |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| Initial identity | 15.4218571566 | Baseline; `3263a928d9624cfbb0be85c34446d5df` |\n| Robust pooled + shrunken sensor linear residuals | 15.0648913575 | Retained then superseded; `86c1af606caf48f8ad79203a3d515352` |\n| Direct pooled absolute-error tree, 90 stages | 14.1452638897 | Retained; `2e850e3255814271aedf8c3397fc72d6` |\n| Longer 180-stage tree | 14.1455193190 | Rejected; global network context also failed local checks |\n| Resumed unchanged 90-stage tree | 14.1452638897 | Exact baseline reproduction; `39b122c311e84d9298e53c94ccdb635d` |\n| Learned sensor-neighborhood tree | 14.1214289791 | Retained; `9b7a1e7ffa6d49ad94b5448f35c9077c` |\n| Neighbor tree + robust sensor affine residual correction | 14.1433545829 | Rejected despite small local gains; `2288d6c5bc914beeaedbd3389753b630` |\n| Anchor-aligned seasonal history innovations | 14.1209047365 | Narrow gain, retained then superseded; `bc4256455f4b4255a911befda3325853` |\n| Partially pooled two-group horizon trees | 14.1101708074 | Retained; `3082fe8bae624ee2b876f9c905fd1000` |\n| Horizon trees + 25% smooth residual network | **14.0354537227** | Retained best; `110ddace979f4037be0412f6c41e3886` |\n| Quarter-strength cross-fitted neural correction | Pending | Implemented in `stacked_calibration.py`; candidate entry point while scoring |\n\nEarlier final 90-stage verification `0997c81d47a54797b3da31d2bc5913b8` also reproduced 14.1452638897.\n\n## Local structural experiments\nValues are last / middle masked MAE. Local failures are rejected without unnecessary public evaluation.\n\n- **Learned neighbors:** old tree 13.627767 / 13.315339; neighbors **13.579012 / 13.297705**. Relative-scale additions 13.573422 / 13.322746 were mixed.\n- **Explicit dynamics / profiles** (`dynamics_calibration.py`): lags 13.607527 / 13.328231; profiles 13.594521 / 13.326066; both 13.630091 / 13.304988; robust summaries 13.670597 / 13.296052; both + neighbors 13.600676 / 13.305833. Rejected.\n- **Sensor correction** (`hierarchical_calibration.py`): regularized affine 13.569863 / 13.288325 looked promising but worsened complete public MAE. Offsets alone and three-block cross-fitted affine corrections were weaker. Rejected.\n- **Heteroscedastic residual scaling** (`scaled_calibration.py`): sensor noise scale 13.773086 / 13.370888; square-root flow 13.672228 / 13.435432; flow 13.788117 / 13.554900. Matching sample weights preserved raw absolute-loss objective, but all variants worsened validation. Rejected.\n- **Seasonal innovations** (`seasonal_calibration.py`): fit eight-harmonic ridge anchor template, align to sample anchors, summarize history innovations. Local 13.559227 / 13.308765; neighbor innovations 13.570034 / 13.332818; short-anchor extrapolation 13.588365 / 13.312023. Local-only version barely improved public MAE.\n- **Horizon specialists** (`horizon_calibration.py`): equal pooled/two-group blend **13.563333 / 13.261141**; pure two-group 13.601248 / 13.313063; three-group blend 13.582039 / 13.273343; pure three-group 13.652307 / 13.349729. Selected two-group blend.\n- **Smooth network** (`neural_calibration.py`): initial 30 epochs pure 13.850695 / 14.179204, quarter blend 13.551673 / 13.329344; rejected. Added Fourier clock features, correct standardization, linear skip, 100 epochs: pure 13.732116 / 13.893861; quarter blend **13.452590 / 13.207139**; half blend 13.453297 / 13.305152. Selected quarter blend; local network fits about 21 seconds.\n- **Origin-bootstrap trees** (`bagged_calibration.py`): three Poisson bootstrap trees replace half the pooled component; blend 13.462832 / 13.208652, full replacement 13.477996 / 13.219142 versus retained 13.452590 / 13.207139. Rejected.\n- **Public physical graph** (`physical_calibration.py`): public adjacency has 548 directed links, all 170 nodes connected. Replace learned graph in horizon trees 13.570624 / 13.270201; append physical context 13.556782 / 13.266412. Augmented network/tree blend 13.480722 / 13.214439, worse than retained on both blocks. Rejected; default graph calculations remain unchanged.\n- **Cross-fitted stacking** (`stacked_calibration.py`): three contiguous-block tree fits supply out-of-fold forecasts as neural base; full-calibration trees are corrected at prediction. Quarter correction **13.430840 / 13.203068**, half 13.414443 / 13.306279, full 13.690142 / 13.942144. Quarter strength improves both blocks; local fits 27-30 seconds. Complete scoring pending.\n\n## Next discriminating experiment\nFirst resolve current stacking public result, retain/revert by complete MAE, and rerun the best entry point. Next research: condition the smooth correction or ensemble weight on horizon and anchor/history disagreement, fitting only from calibration out-of-fold errors with strong shrinkage. Compare against the retained constant blend on the same origin blocks and complete seed protocol; keep fitting below 180 seconds per seed and reuse existing source files if the 16-file limit is reached.\n\n---NOTES---\n{\n  \"policy_name\": \"horizon_tree_smooth_network_blend\",\n  \"method_summary\": \"Blends partially pooled short/long-horizon median residual trees with a small sensor-embedding NumPy network trained on smooth absolute error; both use local history and learned sensor-neighborhood context, and the network adds periodic clock features and a linear correction path. Complete protected MAE is 14.0354537227 for seeds 17, 29 and 43, improving horizon trees 14.1101708074, so the 75% tree / 25% network blend is retained.\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
